## Things deliberately NOT redistributed

| Item | Why not | What to do instead |
|---|---|---|
| **Microsoft Visual C++ runtime DLLs** (`msvcp140*`, `vcruntime140*`, …) | Not redistributable under Madeira's licence; Microsoft has its own terms. Upstream calls this out too. | Extract from `vc_redist.x64.exe` into `app/Madeira/x86_64-vcruntime/`, or supply `VCREDIST_B64` to CI. See `docs/BUILDING.md`. |
| **Apple Metal Shader Converter** | Licence-bound Apple developer download. | Not needed for a normal build: the library is already tracked in the repo. Only a converter *rebuild* needs it. |
| **Any Windows browser binary** | The brief's Variant A wanted a preinstalled Windows browser. This patch ships a native WebKit browser instead (rationale in the file header). Shipping a real Windows browser PE would be a redistribution question for that browser's own licence. | `WindowsBrowser.packageSlot` is an empty extension point. If filled, Firefox (MPL-2.0) is the obvious redistribution-safe choice. |
| **Ubuntu rootfs** | Not built or bundled here. | Ubuntu images are freely redistributable (their licences permit it), but none is included in this patch. |
| **AGPL StikDebug source** | Would force this fork to AGPL. | Not needed. StikJIT (MPL-2.0) provides the same capability and upstream already embeds it. |

## Compatibility conclusion

GPL-3.0-or-later + Madeira Converter Exception + MPL-2.0 (StikJIT) +
MIT/0BSD/LGPL/Apache-2.0 (everything else) is a compatible combination. The
Madeira Converter Exception exists precisely so the project can work with
Apple's Metal Shader Converter while staying GPL; nothing in this patch disturbs
that arrangement.

Had StikDebug's AGPL code been embedded, the fork would have had to become
AGPL-3.0. That was avoidable, so it was avoided. If a future change does need
StikDebug itself rather than StikJIT, this file must be revisited and the whole
fork relicensed to AGPL-3.0.